---

<Layout title="Cory Schulz - Senior Front-End Engineer & Tech Lead">
	<a class="skip-link" href="#experience">Skip to content</a>

	<main id="top">
		<!-- ============ HERO ============ -->
		<!-- No py-section here: .hero rides a padding ladder of its own, so the
		     utility would only be overridden. -->
		<section class="hero">
			<!-- Decorative and deliberately full-bleed: it sits outside the
			     container so it keeps sizing off the section, not the text column. -->
			<svg class="constellation" viewBox="0 0 1200 360" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
				<circle class="twinkle twinkle-a" cx="80" cy="60" r="1.6" fill="var(--gold)"></circle>
				<circle cx="220" cy="180" r="1.1" fill="var(--cream)" opacity="0.5"></circle>
				<circle class="twinkle twinkle-b" cx="360" cy="40" r="1.3" fill="var(--cream)" opacity="0.4"></circle>
				<circle cx="540" cy="120" r="1.0" fill="var(--gold)" opacity="0.6"></circle>
				<circle class="twinkle twinkle-c" cx="700" cy="30" r="1.5" fill="var(--cream)" opacity="0.45"></circle>
				<circle cx="860" cy="150" r="1.2" fill="var(--gold)" opacity="0.7"></circle>
				<circle class="twinkle twinkle-d" cx="1000" cy="70" r="1.6" fill="var(--cream)" opacity="0.4"></circle>
				<circle cx="1120" cy="200" r="1.1" fill="var(--gold)" opacity="0.6"></circle>
				<circle cx="160" cy="300" r="1.2" fill="var(--cream)" opacity="0.35"></circle>
				<circle class="twinkle twinkle-e" cx="1040" cy="310" r="1.3" fill="var(--cream)" opacity="0.4"></circle>
				</svg>

			<!-- Every block below is `relative` on purpose: the constellation above
			     is absolutely positioned, so only a positioned sibling later in the
			     DOM paints over it. -->
			<div class="container flex flex-col items-center text-center">
				<!-- leading-normal because this one wraps to two lines on phones,
				     where fs-overline's line-height: 1 would close them up. -->
				<p class="hero-eyebrow fs-overline text-gold leading-normal text-balance relative mb-[1.75rem]">
					<span>Senior Front-End Engineer &middot; Tech Lead</span>
				</p>

				<h1 class="hero-name fs-heading-1 text-cream relative mb-[2.25rem]">
					<split-text split="chars" trigger="load" stagger="34" duration="900"
						><span class="hero-name-part">Cory</span> <span class="hero-name-part">Schulz</span></split-text
					>
				</h1>

				<p class="fs-subheading text-slate text-pretty relative max-w-[620px] mb-[2.75rem]">
					<split-text
						effect="bloom"
						split="words"
						trigger="load"
						duration="1100"
						stagger="48"
						delay="420"
						>I love to design beautiful experiences and build tools that help other people create more
						amazing things.</split-text
					>
				</p>
				<div class="hero-actions relative flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-[1.25rem]">
					<a class="pill pill-gold" href="#contact" data-scroll-to-contact>Send a Message</a>
					<a
						class="pill pill-outline"
						href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/cory-schulz/"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer">
						LinkedIn
						<svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
							<path
								d="M7 17 L17 7 M9 7 L17 7 L17 15"
								stroke="var(--gold)"
								stroke-width="2"
								stroke-linecap="round"
								stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
						</svg>
					</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- ============ ABOUT ============ -->
		<!-- An interstitial beat between the hero and Experience: no big section
		     title, no top hairline, so it reads as a continuation of the hero
		     rather than the first headline section.

		     No py-section: this beat runs at roughly 60% of the section rhythm and
		     has no tail at all. The stat band ends it and Experience's own top
		     padding carries the seam, which keeps the tiles out of a double gap.
		     Still a clamp, so no rendered size moves. -->
		<section class="section-about" id="about">
			<div
				class="container flex flex-col items-center text-center gap-[0.875rem] reveal reveal-fade-up reveal-delay-500"
			>
				<p class="fs-overline text-gold mb-[0.375rem]">A Little About Me</p>

				<p class="fs-subheading text-slate text-pretty max-w-[620px]">
					I&rsquo;m the creator of Magic Spells, an open-source suite of web components, and Tarot, a
					carousel with real physics. I&rsquo;ve been building for the web for over twenty years. I love working in Figma as
					much as I do in code, and I care a lot about design systems.
				</p>

				<p class="fs-subheading text-slate text-pretty max-w-[620px]">
					I&rsquo;ve also hired and built front-end teams from the ground up. At Pura I hired and
					trained the team, then led the full rebuild of pura.com. The relaunch doubled the
					site&rsquo;s conversion rate, and Shopify wrote a
					<a
						class="about-link"
						href="https://www.shopify.com/case-studies/pura-scents"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer">case study</a
					> on it.
				</p>

				<!-- A display band of four tiles, wider than the text column above it.
				     The numerals are static at their final values — the only motion here
				     is the tiles' staggered rise, which the reveal group drives. -->
				<ul class="stat-line grid grid-cols-4 gap-md w-full max-w-[1080px] mt-[clamp(2.5rem,5vw,3.75rem)]">
					{
						heroStats.map((s) => (
							<li
								class="stat flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-sm px-md py-[clamp(1.75rem,3.2vw,2.5rem)] reveal reveal-fade-up"
								data-reveal-group="stats:100"
							>
								<span class="stat-num">{s.num}</span>
								<span class="stat-label text-slate-dim">{s.label}</span>
							</li>
						))
					}
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- ============ TIMELINE ============ -->
		<section class="py-section section-timeline" id="experience">
			<!-- Desktop: scroll-scrubbed horizontal strip. The heading rides inside
			     the pinned area so it stays with the strip while it scrubs. -->
			<div class="tl-scroll" id="tl-scroll">
				<div class="tl-pin">
					<div class="container">
						<div
							class="flex flex-col items-center gap-md text-center mb-section-head reveal reveal-fade-up">
							<p class="fs-overline text-gold">2013&ndash;Today</p>
							<h2 class="section-title fs-heading-2 text-cream text-balance">
								<split-text effect="rise" split="chars" stagger="26" duration="820"
									>Experience</split-text
								>
							</h2>
							<p class="fs-body-lg text-slate-dim text-pretty max-w-[560px]">
								From a Fortune 500 rewrite to a billion-dollar tequila brand to founding a web app
								framework and an open-source component library.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>
					<!-- The strip is deliberately NOT in the container: it is full-bleed
					     to the section gutters so the scrub keeps the widest possible
					     runway. .tl-viewport takes its gutters as margins (not padding)
					     because the scrub measures travel from its clientWidth. -->
					<div class="tl-viewport" id="tl-viewport">
						<div class="tl-strip" id="tl-strip">
							<div class="tl-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
							{
								stops.map((s) => (
									<article class="tl-stop">
										{s.img ? (
											<img class="tl-media" src={s.img} alt={s.alt} loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
										) : s.logo ? (
											<div class="tl-media tl-media-brand" style={`background:${s.logoBg}`}>
												<img
													class="tl-brand-logo"
													src={s.logo}
													alt={s.alt}
													loading="lazy"
													decoding="async"
												/>
											</div>
										) : (
											<div class="tl-media tl-media-mark">
												<svg
													class="ms-logo"
													viewBox="0 0 1193 238"
													role="img"
													aria-label="Magic Spells">
													<path d={MS_LOGO} fill="currentColor" />
												</svg>
											</div>
										)}
										<svg class="tl-node" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18" aria-hidden="true">
											<path d={STAR} fill={s.img ? 'var(--gold)' : 'var(--gold-bright)'} />
										</svg>
										<div class="tl-text">
											<p class="tl-year">{s.year}</p>
											<h3 class="tl-company">{s.company}</h3>
											<p class="tl-role">{s.role}</p>
											<p class="tl-desc">{s.desc}</p>
										</div>
									</article>
								))
							}
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Mobile: ledger rows -->
			<div class="container tl-ledger-wrap">
				<ol class="tl-ledger">
					{
						stops.map((s) => (
							<li class="tl-ledger-row reveal reveal-fade-up" data-reveal-group="ledger:70">
								<p class="tl-row-year">{s.shortYear}</p>
								<div class="tl-row-body">
									<h3 class="tl-row-company">{s.company}</h3>
									<p class="tl-row-role">{s.role}</p>
									<p class="tl-row-desc">{s.desc}</p>
								</div>
								{s.img ? (
									<img class="tl-row-thumb" src={s.img} alt={s.alt} loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
								) : s.logo ? (
									<div class="tl-row-thumb tl-media-brand" style={`background:${s.logoBg}`}>
										<img
											class="tl-brand-logo"
											src={s.logo}
											alt={s.alt}
											loading="lazy"
											decoding="async"
										/>
									</div>
								) : (
									<div class="tl-row-thumb tl-media-mark">
										<svg
											class="ms-logo ms-logo-sm"
											viewBox="0 0 1193 238"
											role="img"
											aria-label="Magic Spells">
											<path d={MS_LOGO} fill="currentColor" />
										</svg>
									</div>
								)}
							</li>
						))
					}
				</ol>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- ============ TOOLS ============ -->
		<!-- A light interstitial like About: an overline header and the marquee,
		     no display-size title. The rows are full-bleed, so they sit outside
		     the container the header uses. -->
		<section class="py-section" id="tools">
			<div class="container">
				<div
					class="flex flex-col items-center gap-md text-center mb-section-head reveal reveal-fade-up">
					<p class="fs-overline text-gold">Everyday Stack</p>
					<h2 class="section-title fs-heading-2 text-cream text-balance">
						<split-text effect="rise" split="chars" stagger="26" duration="820">Tools I use</split-text>
					</h2>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="flex flex-col gap-3.5 reveal reveal-fade-up">
				{
					[
						{ row: toolRowA, direction: 'left', speed: 26 },
						{ row: toolRowB, direction: 'right', speed: 21 },
					].map(({ row, direction, speed }) => (
						<scrolling-content
							class="tools-marquee"
							direction={direction}
							speed={String(speed)}
							fade="6rem">
							<scrolling-track>
								{row.map((tool) => (
									<div
										class={`tool-tile flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-xs size-27 p-xs rounded-xl${tool.path ? '' : ' tool-tile-text'}`}>
										{tool.path ? (
											<svg
												class="tool-mark size-6.5 text-cream"
												viewBox="0 0 24 24"
												role="img"
												aria-label={tool.name}
												focusable="false">
												<path d={tool.path} fill="currentColor" />
											</svg>
										) : (
											<span class="tool-wordmark font-mono fs-body-sm tracking-[0.01em] text-cream text-center">
												{tool.name}
											</span>
										)}
										<span class="tool-label fs-body-xs text-slate-dim text-center">{tool.name}</span>
									</div>
								))}
							</scrolling-track>
						</scrolling-content>
					))
				}
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- ============ THINGS I'VE BUILT ============ -->
		<section class="py-section section-projects" id="projects">
			<div class="container container-wide">
				<div
					class="flex flex-col items-center gap-md text-center mb-section-head reveal reveal-fade-up">
					<p class="fs-overline text-gold">Free &amp; Open Source</p>
					<h2 class="section-title fs-heading-2 text-cream text-balance">
						<split-text effect="rise" split="chars" stagger="26" duration="820"
							>Things I&rsquo;ve built</split-text
						>
					</h2>
				</div>

				<div class="flex flex-col">
					<!-- ---------- TAROT ---------- -->
					<article class="proj-row grid grid-cols-1 items-center gap-8 py-12 lg:py-20 lg:gap-12 reveal reveal-fade-up" data-reveal-group="projects:110">
						<div class="proj-copy flex flex-col items-start gap-3.5 min-w-0">
							<a class="proj-pill inline-block rounded-full px-3.5 py-1.5 fs-mono-label tracking-[0.14em] text-gold" href="https://magicspells.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
								>magicspells.io/tarot</a
							>
							<h3 class="proj-title fs-heading-3 text-cream">
								<split-text effect="bloom" split="chars" duration="700" stagger="35"
									>Tarot</split-text
								>
							</h3>
							<p class="fs-subheading font-semibold text-cream text-balance">A carousel with real physics.</p>
							<p class="proj-desc fs-body-md text-slate-dim text-pretty max-w-[46ch]">
								A springy, scrubbable carousel that you can throw, catch, and scrub by hand. Every
								frame is driven by a real spring, not a CSS transition.
							</p>
							<ul class="flex flex-col gap-1.5 mt-0.5">
								{
									tarotSpecs.map((spec) => (
										<li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-cream">
											<svg class="flex-none size-3" viewBox="0 0 18 18" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
												<path d={STAR} fill="var(--gold)" />
											</svg>
											<span>{spec}</span>
										</li>
									))
								}
							</ul>
							<p class="mt-1.5 fs-body-sm text-slate-dim">Free to use. Find it at magicspells.io</p>
						</div>
						<div class="proj-demo-tarot min-w-0">
							<tarot-carousel>
								<script type="application/json" data-tarot-options>
									{
										"effect": "peacock",
										"goToSelectedSlide": true,
										"initialIndex": 2,
										"loop": true,
										"gap": 20,
										"paddingLeft": "18%",
										"paddingRight": "18%",
										"slidesPerView": 1,
										"navigation": {
											"showButtons": true,
											"smartButtons": false,
											"showPagination": true
										}
									}
								</script>
								<tarot-viewport>
									<tarot-track>
										{
											tarotSlides.map((s) => (
												<tarot-slide class="tarot-mini-slide">
													{/* w-tarot-slide pins the content to --tarot-slide-width so peacock
													    can animate the slide open around it without squashing the card. */}
													<div class="w-tarot-slide tarot-mini-inner">
														<img src={s.img} alt={s.alt} loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
													</div>
												</tarot-slide>
											))
										}
									</tarot-track>
								</tarot-viewport>
							</tarot-carousel>
						</div>
					</article>

					<!-- ---------- PUZZLE ---------- -->
					<article class="proj-row grid grid-cols-1 items-center gap-8 py-12 lg:py-20 lg:gap-12 reveal reveal-fade-up" data-reveal-group="projects:110">
						<div class="proj-copy flex flex-col items-start gap-3.5 min-w-0">
							<a
								class="proj-pill inline-block rounded-full px-3.5 py-1.5 fs-mono-label tracking-[0.14em] text-gold"
								href="https://github.com/magic-spells/puzzle"
								target="_blank"
								rel="noopener noreferrer">@magic-spells/puzzle</a
							>
							<h3 class="proj-title fs-heading-3 text-cream">
								<split-text effect="bloom" split="chars" duration="700" stagger="35"
									>Puzzle</split-text
								>
							</h3>
							<p class="fs-subheading font-semibold text-cream text-balance">Built to compete with React, Vue, and Svelte.</p>
							<p class="proj-desc fs-body-md text-slate-dim text-pretty max-w-[46ch]">
								A front-end web app framework: single-file <code>.pzl</code> components, reactive data,
								and a Go + esbuild compiler.
							</p>
							<ul class="flex flex-col gap-1.5 mt-0.5">
								{
									puzzleSpecs.map((spec) => (
										<li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-cream">
											<svg class="flex-none size-3" viewBox="0 0 18 18" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
												<path d={STAR} fill="var(--gold)" />
											</svg>
											<span>{spec}</span>
										</li>
									))
								}
							</ul>
							<p class="proj-install mt-1.5 rounded-[10px] px-4.5 py-3 font-mono fs-body-sm text-cream max-w-full overflow-x-auto whitespace-nowrap"><span class="text-gold mr-1.5">$</span> npm i @magic-spells/puzzle</p>
							<a
								class="proj-demo-link inline-flex items-center gap-xs self-start mt-0.5 rounded-full px-4.5 py-2 fs-body-sm font-medium text-cream"
								href="https://puzzle-music-demo.vercel.app/"
								target="_blank"
								rel="noopener noreferrer">
								Preview the music app
								<svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
									<path
										d="M7 17 L17 7 M9 7 L17 7 L17 15"
										stroke="var(--gold)"
										stroke-width="2"
										stroke-linecap="round"
										stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
								</svg>
							</a>
						</div>
						<div class="proj-demo flex items-center justify-center p-7 min-h-75 overflow-hidden min-w-0">
							<pre class="code-card"><code><span class="c-punc">&lt;</span><span class="c-tag">puzzle-view</span><span class="c-punc">&gt;</span>
  <span class="c-punc">&lt;</span><span class="c-tag">button</span> <span class="c-attr">class</span>=<span class="c-str">"counter"</span> <span class="c-evt">@click</span>=<span class="c-bind">&#123; increment &#125;</span><span class="c-punc">&gt;</span>
    Clicked <span class="c-bind">&#123; count &#125;</span> times
  <span class="c-punc">&lt;/</span><span class="c-tag">button</span><span class="c-punc">&gt;</span>
<span class="c-punc">&lt;/</span><span class="c-tag">puzzle-view</span><span class="c-punc">&gt;</span>

<span class="c-punc">&lt;</span><span class="c-tag">script</span><span class="c-punc">&gt;</span>
  <span class="c-kw">export default</span> &#123;
    <span class="c-fn">data</span>: () <span class="c-kw">=&gt;</span> (&#123; <span class="c-attr">count</span>: <span class="c-num">0</span> &#125;),
    <span class="c-fn">increment</span>() &#123;
      <span class="c-kw">this</span>.<span class="c-fn">setData</span>(&#123; <span class="c-attr">count</span>: <span class="c-kw">this</span>.<span class="c-fn">getData</span>().count + <span class="c-num">1</span> &#125;);
    &#125;,
  &#125;;
<span class="c-punc">&lt;/</span><span class="c-tag">script</span><span class="c-punc">&gt;</span></code></pre>
						</div>
					</article>

					<!-- ---------- TIMELINE ENGINE ---------- -->
					<article class="proj-row grid grid-cols-1 items-center gap-8 py-12 lg:py-20 lg:gap-12 reveal reveal-fade-up" data-reveal-group="projects:110">
						<div class="proj-copy flex flex-col items-start gap-3.5 min-w-0">
							<a
								class="proj-pill inline-block rounded-full px-3.5 py-1.5 fs-mono-label tracking-[0.14em] text-gold"
								href="https://github.com/magic-spells/timeline-engine"
								target="_blank"
								rel="noopener noreferrer">@magic-spells/timeline-engine</a
							>
							<h3 class="proj-title fs-heading-3 text-cream">
								<split-text effect="bloom" split="chars" duration="700" stagger="35"
									>Timeline Engine</split-text
								>
							</h3>
							<p class="fs-subheading font-semibold text-cream text-balance">Choreography you can scrub.</p>
							<p class="proj-desc fs-body-md text-slate-dim text-pretty max-w-[46ch]">
								Group animation scenes in a timeline. Drive the timeline with scroll position, scroll
								trigger, or scrub events. Loop scenes, randomize positions, and use physics based
								animations.
							</p>
							<p class="proj-install mt-1.5 rounded-[10px] px-4.5 py-3 font-mono fs-body-sm text-cream max-w-full overflow-x-auto whitespace-nowrap"><span class="text-gold mr-1.5">$</span> npm i @magic-spells/timeline-engine</p>
						</div>
						<div class="proj-demo flex items-center justify-center p-7 min-h-75 overflow-hidden min-w-0 proj-demo-bare" id="fireworks-mount"></div>
					</article>

					<!-- ---------- SPLIT TEXT ---------- -->
					<article class="proj-row grid grid-cols-1 items-center gap-8 py-12 lg:py-20 lg:gap-12 reveal reveal-fade-up" data-reveal-group="projects:110">
						<div class="proj-copy flex flex-col items-start gap-3.5 min-w-0">
							<a
								class="proj-pill inline-block rounded-full px-3.5 py-1.5 fs-mono-label tracking-[0.14em] text-gold"
								href="https://github.com/magic-spells/split-text"
								target="_blank"
								rel="noopener noreferrer">@magic-spells/split-text</a
							>
							<h3 class="proj-title fs-heading-3 text-cream">
								<split-text effect="bloom" split="chars" duration="700" stagger="35"
									>Split Text</split-text
								>
							</h3>
							<p class="fs-subheading font-semibold text-cream text-balance">Text that makes an entrance.</p>
							<p class="proj-desc fs-body-md text-slate-dim text-pretty max-w-[46ch]">
								A web component that splits a line into words, characters, or measured lines and animates
								each unit on a CSS-driven stagger. Eight built-in effects, no dependencies, and no
								framework to adopt. Drop the tag around your copy and it reveals itself when it scrolls
								into view.
							</p>
							<p class="proj-install mt-1.5 rounded-[10px] px-4.5 py-3 font-mono fs-body-sm text-cream max-w-full overflow-x-auto whitespace-nowrap"><span class="text-gold mr-1.5">$</span> npm i @magic-spells/split-text</p>
						</div>
